  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 6.88,
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Welcome, in this short lesson, we will learn what happens when an acid meets a base, this reaction is called neutralization."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.84,
      "end": 16.88,
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Before any experiment, a chemist puts on protective gear, a lab coat, gloves, and safety goggles, acids and bases can burn the skin and the eyes."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.74,
      "end": 24.46,
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Here we pour a solution into a beaker, an acid, like hydrochloric acid, releases hydrogen ions in water,"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.46,
      "end": 31.08,
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "a base, like sodium hydroxide, releases hydroxide ions, combine the two solutions slowly."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.02,
      "end": 37.06,
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "As we stir, each hydrogen ion joins a hydroxide ion to form a molecule of water,"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.38,
      "end": 40.64,
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "the sodium and chloride ions that remain form table salt,"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.0,
      "end": 45.5,
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "so sodium hydroxide plus hydrochloric acid gives sodium chloride and water."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.34,
      "end": 51.46,
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "An indicator tells us when the reaction is complete, when exactly enough base has been added,"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.46,
      "end": 58.14,
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "the solution reaches pH 7, which is neutral. Accidents can happen, if a glass container"
    },
    {
      "start": 58.14,
      "end": 63.92,
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "breaks, never pick up the shards with your hands, tell your teacher, and use a brush and a dust pan."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.76,
      "end": 69.7,
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "To summarize, an acid plus a base gives a salt plus water, this is neutralization,"
    },
    {
      "start": 70.08,
      "end": 73.84,
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "and it is used in everything from antacid tablets to treating acidic soil."
    }
  ],
